#### Support for Non-JSON Artifacts?
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

For non-JSON artifacts, output typically doesn't need to be *input* somewhere else in the same pipeline, and you can just dump the content on the filesystem anywhere you like as usual because [tool containers share the project directory]({{_}}/raw-docker/#tool-container-defaults).  

So.. unless you want [build pipelines]({{_}}/demos/workflows/) then there's little advantage if `compose.mk` gets in the middle.  Plus, while jamming base64 binary data directly into the JSON isn't really recommended.. ipynb's do it all the time! :) 

If you think you *do* have a use-case for something like this you might want to [look at the packaging docs]({{_}}/demos/packaging/), which can at least help with creating archives.

